==Russian==
{{wikipedia|lang=ru}}

===Etymology===
{{af|ru|байда́ра|-ка}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|байда́рка}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Cinemantique-байдарка.wav}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|байда́рка|*}}

# [[kayak]]

====Usage notes====
Russian has two terms for [[kayak]]: {{m|ru|байда́рка}} and {{m|ru|кая́к}}. They are partly synonymous, but are typically used in different contexts:
* {{m|ru|байда́рка}} is typically used for traditional Chukchi, Aleut, and Inuit kayaks, and for modern kayaks which have a frame or are inflatable, especially if designed for flatwater touring;
* {{m|ru|кая́к}} is typically used for modern rigid plastic kayaks, especially if designed for whitewater use and performing [[Eskimo roll]]s.

